      "message": "Netty empties a pipeline once the channel is closed and deregistered, so this get() returns null for any route still in flight when the session goes down, and write()\u0027s catch then logs a NullPointerException stack trace per queued message instead of the ClosedChannelException the old code produced. Could the helper check for null and throw something that names the cause, so a flap during a route push does not fill the log with NPEs that look like a defect?",
